From 9db6fe12a28ab6644544c9c3f9c303cb135025b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lars Grahmann <lars.grahmann@googlemail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:19:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 09/15] synaptics_tudor: Fix pairing loss, session handling and
 slot exhaustion

The pairing is only replaced when the sensor answers the handshake with a
certificate alert, and the old file is kept as .pairing.old. The directory
has to be writable before the sensor is paired and a failed save fails
the open. Command transfers no longer take the cancellable, a failure
inside the session marks it dead so later commands fail fast. A failed
open ends the session and frees everything.

Enroll checks for free slots first and reclaims deleted ones with the
cleanup the vendor driver runs after a delete, otherwise it fails with
DATA_FULL. Delete does the cleanup too and maps a missing template to
DATA_NOT_FOUND. List reads the payload so username, finger and date come
back, clear_storage deletes every template, finger status is reported.

Also: only status 0 is success, bad prints are refused up front, the
enroll capture count is capped, TLS results and randomness are checked,
secrets are cleansed and tudor_cmd_allowed is static. A seed makes every
random value reproducible for emulation and tests.
